{"base_rate":0.17871759890859482,"brier":0.06237025920873124,"bss":0.5750696888235145,"bss_hi":0.65960621921071,"bss_lo":0.4689842697680895,"chart":{"base":[293.7,45.0],"fp":[215.4,369.4],"lead":"62,266.8 272,242.2 482,204.5 692,146.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.58 — higher than 97% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end -0pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 75% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 3%; promised 70% → rained 72%"},"rel":"62,454.8 115,435.9 505.4,156.2"},"country":"MA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.0254570259208731,"ess":251.7924608795067,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Casablanca</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Casablanca rain forecast is strongly skilful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (91%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 733 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 24.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.58, ranked 6 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(2&ndash;31) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>423</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>88</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Casablanca</b> <span class=\"muted\">Morocco</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.58</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>2&ndash;31\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>733 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Casablanca &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Casablanca\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 70.87272727272727,353.04545454545456 109.02657142857143,298.8 237.8044155844156,159.8181818181818 378.3936,32.56 378.3936,76.24000000000001 237.8044155844156,235.45454545454544 109.02657142857143,356.0 70.87272727272727,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"316.94679399727147\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"316.94679399727147\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,372.5342789598109 70.87272727272727,365.45454545454544 109.02657142857143,345.6 237.8044155844156,183.45454545454547 378.3936,56.826666666666654\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 423 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"372.5342789598109\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 88 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"70.87272727272727\" cy=\"365.45454545454544\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"109.02657142857143\" cy=\"345.6\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"237.8044155844156\" cy=\"183.45454545454547\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 91%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"378.3936\" cy=\"56.826666666666654\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(18%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Casablanca the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.62) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.03).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>0.030</td><td class='num'>1.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>0.482</td><td class='num'>1.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>200</td><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'>0.558</td><td class='num'>1.5%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.622</td><td class='num'>3.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":33.58831,"lon":-7.61138,"n":733,"n_cities":213,"name":"Casablanca","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":423,"obs":0.026004728132387706,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03636363636363637,"n":88,"obs":0.045454545454545456,"sig":false},{"hi":0.28,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.14414285714285713,"n":70,"obs":0.1,"sig":false},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.28,"mean":0.507922077922078,"n":77,"obs":0.5454545454545454,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.9050666666666666,"n":75,"obs":0.8933333333333333,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":24.6,"provisional":false,"rank":6,"rank_hi":31.024999999999977,"rank_lo":2.0,"reliability":0.0007483224144646442,"resolution":0.08256246790814838,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"casablanca","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Casablanca"}